description:
Compare a recorded session against a golden transcript (lesson 6.04), after normalising the fields that change from run to run:

```cpp
std::string normalise(const std::string& line, std::map<std::string, std::string>& ids);
std::optional<std::string> firstDifference(const std::vector<std::string>& golden, const std::vector<std::string>& actual);
```

A transcript line looks like `+12ms c>s REQUEST id=41 method=open path=a.md`.

- **normalise**:
  - drops a leading timestamp token (one that starts with `+` and ends with `ms`);
  - replaces the value of every `id=` field with a stable name: the first distinct id seen becomes `#1`, the next `#2`, and so on, using the `ids` map so the same id gets the same name on every line;
  - leaves everything else as it is, with single spaces between tokens.
- **firstDifference** normalises both transcripts (each with its own id map) and compares line by line. It returns `std::nullopt` if they match, or a description: `line N: expected "...", got "..."` (normalised lines, N counting from 1), or for different lengths `line N: expected "...", got end of transcript` / `line N: expected end of transcript, got "..."`.

